    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a proposal for a new high-density residential complex in a fairly established metro area. I need to prep for a town hall meeting with the locals. Can you give me a rundown of the main criticisms or pushback we're probably going to get regarding the zoning changes?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should definitely prepare for strong opposition regarding increased traffic and strain on local infrastructure like schools and water, as high-density development always highlights these concerns first.\n\nNIMBY (Not In My Back Yard) sentiment will likely focus on the perceived \"loss of neighborhood character\" and concerns about the overwhelming of the community feel.\n\nBe ready to defend the design for its scale and how it will benefit the surrounding area, such as through new tax revenue or improved walkability.\n\nProactively address these predictable issues in your proposal to show you have genuinely considered the community's perspective upfront.",
